{"id":"mahabharata-7-155","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":155,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 155 · Krishna rejoices at the rakshasa's fall","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas grieve at the fall of Ghatotkacha, but Krishna roars with joy and tells Arjuna that Karna's divine spear, saved for Arjuna, is now spent. He recounts how Indra gave it for Karna's earrings and armour.","kn":"ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚನ ಪತನಕ್ಕೆ ಪಾಂಡವರು ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಆದರೆ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಹರ್ಷದಿಂದ ಗರ್ಜಿಸಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗಾಗಿ ಉಳಿಸಿಕೊಂಡಿದ್ದ ಕರ್ಣನ ದಿವ್ಯ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಈಗ ವ್ಯರ್ಥವಾಯಿತೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಣನ ಕುಂಡಲ, ಕವಚಕ್ಕೆ ಬದಲಾಗಿ ಇಂದ್ರ ನೀಡಿದ್ದನ್ನು ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"घटोत्कच के पतन पर पाण्डव शोक करते हैं, पर कृष्ण हर्ष से गरजते हैं और अर्जुन से कहते हैं कि अर्जुन के लिए बचाई कर्ण की दिव्य शक्ति अब व्यर्थ हो गई। वे बताते हैं कि इन्द्र ने कर्ण के कुण्डल-कवच के बदले उसे दिया था।","te":"ఘటోత్కచుని పతనానికి పాండవులు దుఃఖిస్తారు; కానీ కృష్ణుడు ఆనందంతో గర్జించి అర్జునుని కోసం దాచిన కర్ణుని దివ్యశక్తి ఇప్పుడు వ్యర్థమైందని చెబుతాడు. కర్ణుని కుండల కవచాలకు బదులుగా ఇంద్రుడు దాన్ని ఇచ్చాడని వివరిస్తాడు.","ta":"கடோத்கசனின் வீழ்ச்சிக்குப் பாண்டவர் வருந்த, கண்ணன் மகிழ்ந்து முழங்கி, அர்ஜுனனுக்காகக் கர்ணன் வைத்திருந்த தெய்வீக சக்தி இப்போது வீணாயிற்று என்கிறார். இந்திரன் கர்ணனின் குண்டலம், கவசத்துக்கு ஈடாக அதைத் தந்ததை விளக்குகிறார்.","ml":"ഘടോൽക്കചന്റെ വീഴ്ചയിൽ പാണ്ഡവർ ദുഃഖിക്കുന്നു; എന്നാൽ കൃഷ്ണൻ ആർത്തുവിളിച്ച് സന്തോഷം പ്രകടിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനനായി കരുതിവെച്ച കർണ്ണന്റെ ദിവ്യകുന്തം ഇപ്പോൾ നിഷ്ഫലമായെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. കർണ്ണന്റെ കുണ്ഡലങ്ങളും കവചവും പകരമായി ഇന്ദ്രൻ ആ കുന്തം നൽകിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.155; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणवधपर्व","titleEn":"Dronavadha Parva (Slaying of Drona)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"हैडिम्बं निहतं दृष्ट्वा विकीर्णमिव पर्वतम् ।\nपाण्डवा दीनमनसः सर्वे बाष्पाकुलेक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the son of Hidimba fallen like a scattered mountain, the Pandavas were all heavy of heart, their eyes brimming with tears."}},{"n":2,"text":"वासुदेवस्तु हर्षेण महताभिपरिप्लुतः ।\nननाद सिंहवन्नादं व्यथयन्निव भारत ।\nविनद्य च महानादं पर्यष्वजत फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Vasudeva was swept up in great joy. He roared like a lion, O Bharata, as if to shake the world, and after that great roar he embraced Phalguna."}},{"n":3,"text":"स विनद्य महानादमभीशून्संनियम्य च ।\nननर्त हर्षसंवीतो वातोद्धूत इव द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having roared and reined in the horses, he danced in a rush of joy, like a tree tossed by the wind."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो विनिर्भ्राम्य पुनः पार्थमास्फोट्य चासकृत् ।\nरथोपस्थगतो भीमं प्राणदत्पुनरच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, whirling Partha around and slapping his arms again and again, Achyuta, standing on the chariot's seat, shouted once more to Bhima."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रहृष्टमनसं ज्ञात्वा वासुदेवं महाबलम् ।\nअब्रवीदर्जुनो राजन्नातिहृष्टमना इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing Vasudeva of great strength to be in high spirits, Arjuna, who was not himself glad, spoke to him, O king."}},{"n":6,"text":"अतिहर्षोऽयमस्थाने तवाद्य मधुसूदन ।\nशोकस्थाने परे प्राप्ते हैडिम्बस्य वधेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said: This great joy of yours today is out of place, Madhusudana, when grief has come with the killing of the son of Hidimba."}},{"n":7,"text":"विमुखानि च सैन्यानि हतं दृष्ट्वा घटोत्कचम् ।\nवयं च भृशमाविग्ना हैडिम्बस्य निपातनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The armies have turned away, seeing Ghatotkacha slain, and we are deeply troubled at the fall of Hidimba's son."}},{"n":8,"text":"नैतत्कारणमल्पं हि भविष्यति जनार्दन ।\nतदद्य शंस मे पृष्टः सत्यं सत्यवतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"This cannot be a small reason, Janardana. So tell me today, since I ask, best of the truthful."}},{"n":9,"text":"यद्येतन्न रहस्यं ते वक्तुमर्हस्यरिंदम ।\nधैर्यस्य वैकृतं ब्रूहि त्वमद्य मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"If it is no secret, you ought to tell, subduer of enemies. Say why your composure has changed today, Madhusudana."}},{"n":10,"text":"समुद्रस्येव संक्षोभो मेरोरिव विसर्पणम् ।\nतथैतल्लाघवं मन्ये तव कर्म जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think this lightness of yours is as strange as the heaving of the ocean or the moving of Mount Meru, Janardana."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"अतिहर्षमिमं प्राप्तं शृणु मे त्वं धनंजय ।\nअतीव मनसः सद्यः प्रसादकरमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, Dhananjaya, the cause of this great joy of mine, which at once brings the highest peace to my mind."}},{"n":12,"text":"शक्तिं घटोत्कचेनेमां व्यंसयित्वा महाद्युते ।\nकर्णं निहतमेवाजौ विद्धि सद्यो धनंजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know, radiant one, that now Karna has been slain in the battle, for he has been made to lose this spear on Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":13,"text":"शक्तिहस्तं पुनः कर्णं को लोकेऽस्ति पुमानिह ।\nय एनमभितस्तिष्ठेत्कार्त्तिकेयमिवाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is there in the world who could stand against Karna with the spear in his hand, as against Kartikeya in battle?"}},{"n":14,"text":"दिष्ट्यापनीतकवचो दिष्ट्यापहृतकुण्डलः ।\nदिष्ट्या च व्यंसिता शक्तिरमोघास्य घटोत्कचे ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune his armor was taken, by good fortune his earrings were taken, and by good fortune his unfailing spear has been wasted on Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":15,"text":"यदि हि स्यात्सकवचस्तथैव च सकुण्डलः ।\nसामरानपि लोकांस्त्रीनेकः कर्णो जयेद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he still had his armor and earrings, mighty Karna alone could conquer even the three worlds with the gods."}},{"n":16,"text":"वासवो वा कुबेरो वा वरुणो वा जलेश्वरः ।\nयमो वा नोत्सहेत्कर्णं रणे प्रतिसमासितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither Indra, nor Kubera, nor Varuna lord of the waters, nor Yama would dare to face Karna in battle."}},{"n":17,"text":"गाण्डीवमायम्य भवांश्चक्रं वाहं सुदर्शनम् ।\nन शक्तौ स्वो रणे जेतुं तथायुक्तं नरर्षभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if you drew Gandiva and I took up the discus Sudarshana, we two could not defeat in battle that bull among men, so equipped."}},{"n":18,"text":"त्वद्धितार्थं तु शक्रेण मायया हृतकुण्डलः ।\nविहीनकवचश्चायं कृतः परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For your good, Indra took his earrings by a trick and made this conqueror of enemy cities lose his armor."}},{"n":19,"text":"उत्कृत्य कवचं यस्मात्कुण्डले विमले च ते ।\nप्रादाच्छक्राय कर्णो वै तेन वैकर्तनः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because Karna cut off his armor and gave his bright earrings to Indra, he is remembered as Vaikartana."}},{"n":20,"text":"आशीविष इव क्रुद्धः स्तम्भितो मन्त्रतेजसा ।\nतथाद्य भाति कर्णो मे शान्तज्वाल इवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today Karna seems to me like a cobra that was angry but is held still by the power of a mantra, like a fire whose flame has died down."}},{"n":21,"text":"यदा प्रभृति कर्णाय शक्तिर्दत्ता महात्मना ।\nवासवेन महाबाहो प्राप्ता यासौ घटोत्कचे ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the time the great Indra gave the spear to Karna, mighty-armed one, that spear which has now been spent on Ghatotkacha,"}},{"n":22,"text":"कुण्डलाभ्यां निमायाथ दिव्येन कवचेन च ।\nतां प्राप्यामन्यत वृषा सततं त्वां हतं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"in exchange for his earrings and divine armor, Karna, once he had it, kept thinking that you were as good as slain in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवं गतेऽपि शक्योऽयं हन्तुं नान्येन केनचित् ।\nऋते त्वा पुरुषव्याघ्र शपे सत्येन चानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even so he cannot be killed by anyone else but you, tiger among men. I swear it by truth, sinless one."}},{"n":24,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यः सत्यवादी च तपस्वी नियतव्रतः ।\nरिपुष्वपि दयावांश्च तस्मात्कर्णो वृषा स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is devoted to brahmins, truthful, an ascetic of firm vows, and kind even to enemies. Therefore Karna is called Vrisha."}},{"n":25,"text":"युद्धशौण्डो महाबाहुर्नित्योद्यतशरासनः ।\nकेसरीव वने मर्दन्मत्तमातङ्गयूथपान् ।\nविमदान्रथशार्दूलान्कुरुते रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in battle, mighty-armed, always with bow raised, like a lion in the forest crushing herds of rutting elephants, he leaves the tigers among chariot-warriors spiritless at the head of the battle."}},{"n":26,"text":"मध्यंगत इवादित्यो यो न शक्यो निरीक्षितुम् ।\nत्वदीयैः पुरुषव्याघ्र योधमुख्यैर्महात्मभिः ।\nशरजालसहस्रांशुः शरदीव दिवाकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the midday sun, he cannot be looked at by your own great-souled chief warriors, tiger among men. With his thousands of rays of arrow-nets he is like the autumn sun."}},{"n":27,"text":"तपान्ते तोयदो यद्वच्छरधाराः क्षरत्यसौ ।\nदिव्यास्त्रजलदः कर्णः पर्जन्य इव वृष्टिमान् ।\nसोऽद्य मानुषतां प्राप्तो विमुक्तः शक्रदत्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a cloud at the end of summer pours down streams, so Karna, a cloud of divine weapons, a Parjanya of rain, pours arrows. Today he has become merely human, released from Indra's spear."}},{"n":28,"text":"एको हि योगोऽस्य भवेद्वधाय\nछिद्रे ह्येनं स्वप्रमत्तः प्रमत्तम् ।\nकृच्छ्रप्राप्तं रथचक्रे निमग्ने\nहन्याः पूर्वं त्वं तु संज्ञां विचार्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is only one way to kill him: at a gap, when he is off guard and you are alert. When he is in trouble, his chariot wheel sunk, you should strike him first, after considering the signal."}},{"n":29,"text":"जरासंधश्चेदिराजो महात्मा\nमहाबलश्चैकलव्यो निषादः ।\nएकैकशो निहताः सर्व एव\nयोगैस्तैस्तैस्त्वद्धितार्थं मयैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jarasandha, the great-souled king of Chedi, and mighty Ekalavya the Nishada: each of these was killed by me, by such means, for your good."}},{"n":30,"text":"अथापरे निहता राक्षसेन्द्रा\nहिडिम्बकिर्मीरबकप्रधानाः ।\nअलायुधः परसैन्यावमर्दी\nघटोत्कचश्चोग्रकर्मा तरस्वी ॥","meaning":{"en":"And other rakshasa lords were killed, led by Hidimba, Kirmira and Baka, and Alayudha, the crusher of enemy armies, and Ghatotkacha, fierce in deed and swift."}}]}]}